Subject: [PATCH 02256/11362] [outer-loop] open SOTA LLM is a REQUIRED
 escalation tier (verifier-routed cascade), not a TRM alternative

Operator: even with TRM, hard games will need an open SOTA model to help solve. So the
live stack is a verifier-routed CASCADE: tier1 training-free explorer (BFS/DFS) -> tier2
tiny trained TRM-class dynamics (cheap/common) -> tier3 bundled open SOTA LLM (E3 induction
+ goal reasoning) for the hard tail. The Carnot verifier is the ROUTER (detects stall ->
escalate) AND the GROUND (checks the LLM's model before trusting -- the cd82 divergence-
halt). Both TRM and the LLM are bundled. Key budget point: tier3 fires SELECTIVELY (rare
hard games) so its load+inference cost amortizes -> we can afford a STRONGER open model
(gemma-4-26B-A4B / Qwen3.6-35B-A3B) for escalation. Integration: unify explorer-mode +
E3-mode into one verifier-routed choose_action.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
